on-group><article-title>Mdv1p is a WD repeat protein that interacts with the dynamin-related GTPase, Dnm1p, to trigger mitochondrial division</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>151</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>353</fpage><lpage>365</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11038182</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="vanderBliek1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van der Bliek</surname><given-names>A.M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Functional diversity in the dynamin family</article-title><source>Trends Cell Biol</source><volume>9</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>96</fpage><lpage>102</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10201074</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Wongetal2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>E.D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>J.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gorsich</surname><given-names>S.W.</given-names></name><name><surname>McCaffery</surname><given-names>J.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Shaw</surname><given-names>J.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Nunnari</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The dynamin-related GTPase, Mgm1p, is an intermembrane space protein required for maintenance of fusion competent mitochondria</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>151</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>341</fpage><lpage>352</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11038181</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig position="float" id="F1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Possible evolutionary origins of the mitochondrial inner and outer membrane division machineries.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JCB0009102.f1"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Model for the functions of Fis1/Mdv2 and Mdv1/Fis2/Gag3 based on their subcellular localizations and mutant phenotypes. In step 1, Fis1/Mdv2 recruits Dnm1 to the surface of the mitochondrion. In step 2, Mdv1/Fis2/Gag3 is added to the complex. In step 3, the mitochondrial division apparatus, consisting of Dnm1, Mdv1/Fis2/Gag3, and possibly other components, help constrict the mitochondrial outer membrane.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JCB0009102.f2"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>